    "lawCode": "Amd §§490 & 504, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5955A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation\nto  prohibiting  the  imposition  of  any additional fee for a veteran's\ndistinguishing mark on a non-driver identification card  or  a  driver's\nlicense\n\nPURPOSE  OR  GENERAL  IDEA OF BILL:  To prohibit the imposition of addi-\ntional fees for the issuance of a duplicate or amended driver's  license\nor non-driver identification card with a veteran's notation.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:  The bill amends paragraph (b) of subdi-\nvision  3  of  §490  and paragraph (a-1) of subdivision 1 of §504 of the\nVehicle and Traffic Law to prohibit the imposition of any fees  for  the\nduplication  or  amendment  of a nondriver identification (NDID) card or\ndriver's license prior to renewal, if the duplication  or  amendment  is\nsolely  for  the  purpose of adding a veteran distinguishing mark to the\ncard or license.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  Chapter 487 of 2012 directs the DMV to make  the  veter-\nan's  status available to all veterans of the United States Armed Forces\nwho were honorably discharged or were released  under  honorable  condi-\ntions  who  apply for the designation on a DMV-issued NDID card or driv-\ner's license. Currently, veterans would need to pay a $12.50  photo  fee\nto  make  the change prior to the date of renewal. This bill would waive\nthe state photo fee of $12.50 for veterans for the  option  of  amending\ntheir  New  York State driver license, permit, or non-driver identifica-\ntion card, prior to the date of renewal, to indicate their status  as  a\nveteran.\n\nPRIOR  LEGISLATIVE  HISTORY:   2013: Referred to Assembly Transportation\nCommittee.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:  Limited.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect thirty days after  it  shall\nhave become a law.\n\n",
